{
  "total": 304,
  "totalPage": 7,
  "page": 5,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b37d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 349,
      "bookHadithIndex": 201,
      "text": "(Another chain) from Abu Hurairah, :from the Prophet and it is the same or similar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-349-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-349-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b37e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 350,
      "bookHadithIndex": 202,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated:\"The Prophet would perform Salat in sheep pens",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-350-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-350-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-350-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-350-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b37f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 351,
      "bookHadithIndex": 203,
      "text": "Jabir narrated:\"The Prophet dispatched me for something he needed. I came to him while he was performing Salat on his mount, heading east, he made the prostrations lower than the bowing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-351-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-351-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-351-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-351-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b380",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 352,
      "bookHadithIndex": 204,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated:\"The Prophet performed Salat towards his she-camel, or his mount, and he would perform Salat while on his mount, whichever direction it was facing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-352-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-352-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-352-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-352-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b381",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 353,
      "bookHadithIndex": 205,
      "text": "Anas conveyed that :the Prophet said: \"When supper is present and the Iqamah for Salat has been called, then begin with supper",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-353-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-353-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-353-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-353-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b382",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 354,
      "bookHadithIndex": 206,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated that:the Prophet said: \"When the supper is presented and the Iqamah is called for Salat, then begin with the supper",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-354-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b383",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 355,
      "bookHadithIndex": 207,
      "text": "Aishah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \"When one of you is sleepy and he is performing Salat, then let him lie down until the sleep is gone from him. For when one of you performs Salat while he is sleepy, perhaps he wants to seek forgiveness but he curses himself",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-355-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-355-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-355-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-355-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b384",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 356,
      "bookHadithIndex": 208,
      "text": "Abu Atiyyah narrated that :a man among them said: \"Malik bin Al-Huwairith came to us in our Musalla to narrate. One day when it was time for Salat, we told him to go ahead (to lead the prayer). He said: 'Let one of you go forward, until I narrate to you why I would not go forward (to lead prayer): I heard Allah's Messenger saying: \"Whoever visits a people, then he does not lead them, but a man among them leads them",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-356-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-356-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-356-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-356-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b385",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 357,
      "bookHadithIndex": 209,
      "text": "Thawban narrated that :the Prophet said: \"It is not allowed for a man to look into the interior of a man's house until he has been given permission, for if he looks, then he has entered. And one who leads people (in Salat) should not supplicate for himself alone with the exclusion of his congregation. If he does, then he has betrayed them. And one is not to stand for Salat while he has to urinate",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-357-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-357-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-357-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-357-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b386",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 358,
      "bookHadithIndex": 210,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated:\"Allah's Messenger cursed three people: A man who leads people (in Salat) while they dislike him, a woman who spends a night while her husband is angry with her, and a man who hears: 'Hayya Alal Falah (come to success)' then does not respond",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-358-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Very Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-358-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Very Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-358-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-358-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b387",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 359,
      "bookHadithIndex": 211,
      "text": "Amr bin Al-Harith Al-Mustaliq said:\"It used to be said that the people with the worst punishment [on the Day of Judgment] are two: A woman who disobeyed her husband, and a people's Imam whom they dislike",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-359-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-359-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b388",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 360,
      "bookHadithIndex": 212,
      "text": "Abu Umamah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \"There are three whose Salat would not rise up beyond their ears: The runaway slave until he returns, a woman who spends a night while her husband is angry with her, and a people's Imam whom they dislike",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-360-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-360-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-360-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-360-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b389",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 361,
      "bookHadithIndex": 213,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated:\"Allah's Messenger fell from a horse and got injured, so he led Salat sitting and we also offered Salat sitting. When he completed the Salat he said: \"The Imam is appointed to be followed; when he says the Takbir then say the Takbir, when he bows, then bow, and when he raises his head, then raise your heads. When he says: \"Sami' Allahu liman hamidah (Allah listens to those who praise him)\" then say: \"Rabbana wa lakal-hamd. (O our Lord! And all praise is Yours.)\" and when he prostrates, then prostrate, and when he performs Salat sitting, then pray sitting altogether",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-361-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-361-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-361-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-361-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 362,
      "bookHadithIndex": 214,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"Allah's Messenger performed Salat behind Abu Bakr, during the illness from which he died, and he was sitting",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-362-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-362-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-362-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-362-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 363,
      "bookHadithIndex": 215,
      "text": "Anas narrated:\"Allah's Messenger performed Salat during his illness behind Abu Bakr while seated, wrapped in a garment",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-363-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-363-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-363-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-363-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 364,
      "bookHadithIndex": 216,
      "text": "Ash-Sha'bi narrated:\"Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah led us in Salat, and he continued after the two Rak'ah, so the people said: 'Subhan Allah' and he said: 'Subhan Allah' to them. When he finished his Salat he said the Taslim then performed two prostrations of As-Sahw while he was sitting. Then he narrated to them that Allah's Messenger did the same with them as he had done",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-364-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-364-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-364-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 365,
      "bookHadithIndex": 217,
      "text": "Ziyad bin Haqah narrated:\"Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah les us in Salat. When he prayed two Rak'ah he stood without sitting. Those who were behind him said 'Subhan Allah' and he indicated to them that they should stand. He said the Taslim when he had finished his Salat and he performed two prostrations of As-Sahw, and said the Taslim. He said that Allah's Messenger did this",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-365-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-365-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-365-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-365-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 366,
      "bookHadithIndex": 218,
      "text": "Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Mas'ud) that he said:\"When Allah's Messenger sat for the first two Rak'ah it was as if he was on hot stones.\" Shu'bah (one of the narrators) said: \"Then Sa'd's lips moved (saying) something. So I said: 'Until he stood?' He said: 'Until he stood",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-366-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-366-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-366-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b38f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 367,
      "bookHadithIndex": 219,
      "text": "Suhaib narrated:\"I passed by Allah's Messenger (S) while he was performing Salat, so I said greeted him with Salam, and he returned it by making signals.\" He said: \"I do not know except that he said: 'He indicated with his finger",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-367-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-367-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-367-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b390",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 368,
      "bookHadithIndex": 220,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated:\"I said to Bilal: 'How did the Prophet (S) reply to them when they gave him Salams and he was performing Salat?' He said: 'He would motion with his hand",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-368-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-368-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-368-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-368-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b391",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 369,
      "bookHadithIndex": 221,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \"The Tasbih is for the men and clapping is for the women",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-369-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-369-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-369-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-369-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b392",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 370,
      "bookHadithIndex": 222,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\"Yawning in prayer (salah) is from the Shaitan, so when one of you yawns then let him suppress (it) as much as possible",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-370-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-370-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-370-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-370-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b393",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 371,
      "bookHadithIndex": 223,
      "text": "Imran bin Husain narrated:\"I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about the Salat for a man who is sitting. He said: 'Whoever performs Salat while standing then that is more virtuous. And whoever performs Salat while sitting, then he gets half the rewards of the one standing, and whoever performs Salat while lying down, then he gets half the rewards of the one sitting",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-371-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-371-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-371-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-371-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b394",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 372,
      "bookHadithIndex": 224,
      "text": "This Hadith has been related from Ibrahim bin Tahman with this chain. Except that he said:\"From Imran bin Husain who said: 'I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about Salat for a sick person. He said: \"He performs Salat standing, if he is not able then sitting, if he is not able then on his side",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-372-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-372-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b395",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 373,
      "bookHadithIndex": 225,
      "text": "Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet (S), narrated:\"I did not see Allah's Messenger (S) praying voluntary prayers sitting until the year before he died. Then he would perform Salat for the voluntary prayers sitting, and he would recite a Surah and prolong it such that it would be longer than the longest of them",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-373-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-373-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-373-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-373-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b396",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 374,
      "bookHadithIndex": 226,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"The Prophet (S) would perform Salat while sitting. And he would recite while sitting. When about thirty or forty Ayah of his recitation remained he would standup and recite while he was standing, then he would bow and prostrate. Then he would do the same in the second Rak'ah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-374-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-374-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-374-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-374-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b397",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 375,
      "bookHadithIndex": 227,
      "text": "Abdullah bun Shaqiq narrated from Aishah, he said:\"I asked her about the voluntary Salat of Allah's Messenger (S), she said: 'He would pray long into the night standing, and long into the night sitting. So when he recited and he was standing, he would bow and prostrate whole he was standing, and when he recited while he was sitting, he bowed and prostrated while he was sitting",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-375-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-375-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-375-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-375-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b398",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 376,
      "bookHadithIndex": 228,
      "text": "Anas bin Malik narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \"Indeed I hear the crying of a small boy while I am in Salat, so I shorten it in fear that his mother may be tormented",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-376-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-376-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-376-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-376-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b399",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 377,
      "bookHadithIndex": 229,
      "text": "Aishah narrated that:Allah's Messenger said: \"The Salat of a women who has reached the age of menstruation is not accepted without a Khimar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-377-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-377-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-377-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 378,
      "bookHadithIndex": 230,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"Allah's Messenger (S) prohibited As-Sadl in the Salat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-378-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-378-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-378-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 379,
      "bookHadithIndex": 231,
      "text": "Abu Dharr narrated that :the Prophet (S) said: \"When one of you stands for Salat then he should not smoothen the pebbles, for indeed it is mercy that he is facing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-379-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-379-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-379-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-379-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 380,
      "bookHadithIndex": 232,
      "text": "Mu'aiqib narrated:\"I asked Allah's Messenger (S) about smoothening the pebbles during Salat. He said: 'If you must do so, then let it be only once",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-380-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-380-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-380-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-380-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 381,
      "bookHadithIndex": 233,
      "text": "Umm Salamah narrated:\"The Prophet (S) saw a boy of ours - called Aflah - blowing when he prostrated. So he said: 'O Aflah! Put your face in the dirt",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-381-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-381-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-381-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 382,
      "bookHadithIndex": 234,
      "text": "(Another chain) in which Abu Hamzah narrated:\"A boy of ours named Rabah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-382-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b39f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 383,
      "bookHadithIndex": 235,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"The Prophet (S) prohibited than a man to pray with his hands on his hip",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-383-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-383-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-383-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b3a0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 384,
      "bookHadithIndex": 236,
      "text": "Abu Rafi narrated that :He passed by Al-Hasan bin Ali while he was performing Salat and he had gathered his locks at the back of his head, so he (Abu Rafi) undid them, and Al-Hasan turned to him angrily. He said: \"Resume your Salat and do not be angry, for indeed I heard Allah's Messenger (S) saying: 'That is the seat of Ash-Shaitan",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-384-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-384-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-384-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-384-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b3a1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 385,
      "bookHadithIndex": 237,
      "text": "Al-Fadl bin Al-`Abbas narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \"As-Salat is two and two, with a Tashahhud for every two Rak`ah, with humility, imploring, having a sense of tranquility, pleading and showing helplessness and stretching out your hand\" - he said: raising them - \"to your Lord, with the insides of them facing your face, saying: 'O Lord! O Lord! And whoever does not do this, then it is like this or that",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-385-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-385-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-385-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b3a2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 386,
      "bookHadithIndex": 238,
      "text": "Ka'b bun Ujrah narrated that:Allah's Messenger (S) said: \"When one of you performs Wudu and does so well, then he leaves intending to go to the Masjid, then let him not intertwine his fingers, for indeed he is in Salat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-386-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-386-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-386-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-386-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b3a3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 387,
      "bookHadithIndex": 239,
      "text": "Jabir narrated:\"It was said to the Prophet (S): 'Which Salat is most virtuous?' He said: 'That with the longest Qunut",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-387-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-387-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-387-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-387-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b3a4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 388,
      "bookHadithIndex": 240,
      "text": "Ma'dan bin Talhah Al Yamari said:\"I met Thawban the freed slave of Allah's Messenger (S) and said to him, 'Guide me to a deed by which Allah benefit me, and for which Allah will admit me into Paradise.' He was silent for quite a while, then he turned to me and said: 'Perform prostrations, for I heard Allah's Messenger (S) saying: 'No worshipper performs a prostration to Allah except that by it, Allah will raise him a level, and erase a sin from him for it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-388-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
